Z||000004||qwikgta||08-14-2001||11:22 PM||||When you finish the poly make sure to post how easy it was, I have a full front and rear poly set for my 88 that I will do this winter.  Never done it b4 so not sure if its easy or diff.<P>Thanks<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||KissMySSFiero||08-15-2001||07:42 AM||||ive been working on it since sunday.  i got a few hours in mon and tues.  i had to pull the subframe down to fix some stuff from an accident.  if i didnt have to do that i would have been done by now.  its just time consuming.  i used a propane torch to burn out the old bushings.  that took a few minutes each.  also i painted all the parts before i started to put them back.  also i replaced the ball joints,  but that was very simple with a ball joint press.  you dont need it for uppers but dont do it without one for the lowers.  expect bolts to break.  and be prepared to find the replacements.  i got lucky with the lower control arm bolts.  but i broke one of the upper control arm shafts.  i would have rather broke all the lower bolts(much cheaper) if you have any questions email me.   ssfiero@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
